# <%= projectName %>

HTTP-first React SSR starter generated by `fluo new --starter react-vite-ssr`.

## Run

```sh
pnpm install
pnpm typecheck
pnpm test
pnpm build
pnpm start
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:3000/products/sku-42?preview=true`. Run `pnpm test:browser` after
installing the Playwright Chrome browser when you want the production hydration regression.

## Contract

- `src/app.ts` owns HTTP page routing and returns the `ReactElement` created by the JSX renderer in `src/page.tsx`.
- `src/main.ts` loads `dist/client/.vite/manifest.json` explicitly and passes the parsed value to the application module.
- `@fluojs/react/vite` only parses that already-loaded manifest into hydration assets.
- `src/entry-server.ts` and `src/entry-client.tsx` keep server and browser entry boundaries explicit.
- `Link` renders a real anchor, while `router.push(...)` performs full-document navigation through the server-owned route.
- The Fastify asset controller is a minimal local starter boundary. Production deployments should serve `dist/client` through their normal static-file or CDN infrastructure.

This starter intentionally excludes RSC, Server Functions, file routing, a client route table, SPA document swapping, prefetch, and a data cache.
